                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Incorrect. The equilibrium constant is a numerical measure of the ratio of “products over reactants” that indicates the extent to which the reaction favors products or reactants. Reactions with larger equilibrium constants favor more products than reactants compared to reactions with smaller equilibrium constants. Be sure to interpret the negative exponents correctly (larger negative exponents have smaller values)."
